# Local Maven CLI overrides (template).
#
# By default this project pulls the Multicloud DB SDK from Maven Central
# at the version pinned in pom.xml. To test against a locally-built SDK
# (e.g., while developing the SDK itself in multiclouddb-sdk-for-java):
#
#   1. Build & install the SDK locally:
#        cd <multiclouddb-sdk-for-java>
#        mvn clean install -DskipTests
#
#   2. Activate this override:
#        cp .mvn/maven.config.example .mvn/maven.config
#
#   3. Edit .mvn/maven.config and set the versions below to match the
#      version that was installed into your ~/.m2 repository.
#
# Maven reads .mvn/maven.config on every invocation and appends each
# line to the CLI as an argument. One argument per line, no quoting.
#
# .mvn/maven.config is git-ignored so per-developer overrides never
# leak into commits.

-Dmulticlouddb-api.version=0.2.0-SNAPSHOT
-Dmulticlouddb-provider-cosmos.version=0.2.0-SNAPSHOT
-Dmulticlouddb-provider-dynamo.version=0.2.0-SNAPSHOT
-Dmulticlouddb-provider-spanner.version=0.2.0-SNAPSHOT
